More semi-breaking change: extract CellDescriptor return into `_getCells()` (#33)

Every module calls `this._addRow()` in its `_handleEvent()` method. Reduce boilerplate by moving the common case into the base class.

- new method  `_getCells()` returns only the CellDescriptor array/callback
- DataTableModule's base `_handleEvent()` calls `_addRow()` with event and the result of `_getCells()`
- modules can override `_handleEvent()` for special processing or to skip events
- a module that relies on the base `_handleEvent()` must define its own `_getCells()` method

``` javascript
export class FSDJumpModule extends DataTableModule {
	constructor(router, options) {
		super(router, ["journal:fsdjump"], options);
	}

	_getCells(event) {
		return [ event.StarSystem ];
	}
}
```
